{title: Darkness Is My Closest Friend}
{subtitle: Psalm 88}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O Lord, God of my salvation
I cry out day and night before you
Let my [B]prayer come be[F#]fore you
In[B]cline your ear to my [D#m]cry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For my soul is full of troubles
My life draws near to the [C#]grave
I [F#]am counted among those who [C#]go down to the pit
Like [B]the slain that lie in the [D#m]grave
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why do you [B]cast my soul a[F#]way
Why do you [C#]hide your face from [D#m]me
You have [B]caused my friends to [F#]shun me
[C#]Darkness is my closest [D#m]friend
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
But I, O Lord, cry to you
In the morning my prayer comes before [C#]you
I [F#]suffer your terrors, I am [C#]helpless
They surround [B]me like a flood all [C#]day [D#m]long
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why do [B]you cast my soul a[F#]way
Why do you [C#]hide your face from [D#m]me
You have [B]caused my friends to [F#]shun me
[C#]Darkness is my closest [D#m]friend
{end_of_chorus}
